# This is a TEMPLATE, not a live file. Nothing reads it.
#
# Next.js reads `.env.local` (git-ignored, for local development) and, in
# production, whatever you've set in your host's dashboard. If you want to
# override something locally, copy this file to `.env.local` first.
#
# As it stands you don't need either. The project reads exactly one variable,
# and it's optional.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL — optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The canonical origin of the deployed site. No trailing slash.
#
# Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph images, sitemap.xml, robots.txt and the
# JSON-LD. It does NOT affect the contact form.
#
# Unset, it falls back to https://theninjadev.dev — a domain you don't own, so
# your metadata would point somewhere that isn't yours. Set it to wherever the
# site actually lives (your vercel.app URL is fine until you buy a domain).
#
# If you create this in a dashboard, give it a value or delete it. A variable
# that exists but is blank used to crash the build; it no longer does, but it
# still silently gets you the fallback.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-site.vercel.app

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT — optional, almost certainly leave this alone
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The contact form posts to Formspree, who email the submission to you. The
# endpoint is NOT here — it's `contactFormEndpoint` in src/data/site.ts.
#
# That's deliberate. A Formspree endpoint isn't a secret (it's designed to sit
# in public page source, and spam is filtered per-form on their side), so
# keeping it in the repo means a fresh deploy works with nothing to configure.
#
# Set this only to point at a different form without editing code — a staging
# site, say. Accepts the full URL or just the id.
#
# Where things live now:
#   - which address enquiries are delivered to -> the Formspree dashboard
#   - whether the form is wired up at all      -> src/data/site.ts
#   - with no endpoint configured              -> the form falls back to a
#                                                 pre-filled mailto: link
# FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Removed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY, CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL and CONTACT_TO_EMAIL are no longer read
# by anything. Resend only sends from a domain you own and have verified,
# which made it a poor fit before buying one. Delete them from your hosting
# dashboard if you added them.
